package "main"

import "pkg/fvanon"

// Cross-package proof for a small source-level ANONYMOUS-struct func-value arg — the
// arm32 shim <-> LLVM-callee ABI contract for a COERCED aggregate.  Native `main`
// forms a *func value pointing at a CROSS-PACKAGE function (pkg/fvanon.Field,
// LLVM-compiled under `-backend native`) that takes an anonymous struct{ x int }
// (SizeOf 4 on ILP32) BY VALUE, and calls it via func-value dispatch.
//
// A source-level anon struct is COERCED: IR-gen names it `__anon_N`
// (gen_type_resolve.bn), so AggInRegCoercedKind — and AggCoercedInReg — is TRUE, and
// isByAddressAggArm32 is TRUE via branch 1.  Both the native dispatch and the native
// shim pass it BY-ADDRESS (one dispatch pointer word the shim re-expands), matching
// the LLVM callee, which declares the coerced arg i8* / reads it from the same
// coerced [1 x i32] layout.
//
// What is exercised: `main` builds the func value with its OWN native vtable, so the
// call runs native emitCallFuncValue -> native marshaling shim -> the LLVM-compiled
// underlying `Field` (the native shim tail-branches to the extern `Field` symbol; the
// LLVM-emitted @__shim.<Field> is a differently-named weak symbol `main` never
// references).  So this is native-dispatch -> NATIVE-shim -> LLVM-callee; it does NOT
// exercise native-dispatch -> LLVM-EMITTED-shim (1006 covers that).  The native shim
// marshals the coerced anon struct by-address into the LLVM callee's AAPCS32 coerced
// slot, the field round-trips, and 42 comes back.
func main() {
	var v struct { x int }
	v.x = 42
	var f *func(struct { x int }) int = fvanon.Field
	println(f(v)) // 42
}
